cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LocalGovBench, please cite this research software."
type: software
title: "LocalGovBench: Disclosure Affordances in Public AI and Algorithm Registers"
version: 0.2.0
# date-released: set when the GitHub/Zenodo release is published
# USER CONFIRMATION: leave date unset until formal release
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Reproducible research repository for studying schema disclosure affordance
  and planned record-level realization in public AI and algorithm registers,
  using Disclosure Functions v1. Includes a frozen specification layer,
  observed-field schema inventory tooling, and a human schema-coding system.
  Does not provide governance readiness or maturity scores, shortfall scores,
  compliance scores, composite indices, or jurisdiction rankings. Historical
  LocalGovBench v0.1.0 (Governance Readiness Benchmark) remains available as a
  provenance archive (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.20543779) and is not the active
  analytical framework. Full realization analyses, IRR results, gap figures,
  and manuscript outcomes are not claimed complete in this provisional metadata.
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - public sector
  - algorithm registers
  - AI inventories
  - algorithmic transparency
  - disclosure affordance
  - schema coding
  - reproducibility
  - European Union
authors:
  - given-names: César
    family-names: Andrés
    affiliation: >-
      CRIA-BDHS Research Group, Higher Polytechnic School of Technology and
      Science, Universidad Camilo José Cela, Madrid, Spain
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-8968-3404"
    email: cesar.andress@ucjc.edu
repository-code: "https://github.com/cesar-andress/localgovbench"
url: "https://github.com/cesar-andress/localgovbench"
# doi: set to the new Zenodo version DOI when minted for v0.2.0
